00:18:17,142 --> 00:18:23,142
Fessenden (born March 23, 1963) is an American actor and filmmaker.

9
00:20:34,285 --> 00:20:40,285
He is the founder of the New York based independent
production outfit Glass Eye Pix.

10
00:22:51,428 --> 00:22:57,428
His writer/director credits include No Telling (written with Beck Underwood, 1991), Habit (1997), Wendigo (2001), and The Last
Winter (written with Robert Leaver, 2006), which is in the permanent collection of the Museum of Modern Art.

11
00:25:08,571 --> 00:25:14,571
He has also directed the television feature Beneath (2013), an episode of the NBC TV series Fear Itself (2008)
entitled "Skin and Bones", and a segment of the anthology horror-comedy film The ABCs of Death 2 (2014).

12
00:27:25,714 --> 00:27:31,714
He is the writer, with Graham Reznick, of the BAFTA
Award-winning Sony PlayStation video game Until Dawn.

13
00:29:42,857 --> 00:29:48,857
Films he has acted in include Bringing Out the Dead (1999), Broken Flowers (2005), I Sell the Dead (2009), Jug Face (2012), We Are Still Here (2015), In
a Valley of Violence (2016), Like Me (2017), and The Dead Don't Die (2019), Brooklyn 45 (2023), and Killers of the Flower Moon (2023).
